From c6739a4f019a56008526f1fc2fe419410baebab0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tong <zhengtong0611@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 04:59:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 02/13] Referee bridge: bubble beside the head, sizes in screen
 pixels

Two speech_bridge.json options for running several avatars side by side
(the debate's For/Against side bots). Both default to off, which keeps
ME's own bubble spot and units exactly as before.

- screenPixels: fontSize and bubbleWidth (and ME's padding, spacing and
  sprite corners) are screen pixels. The bubble lives on TalkPanel, a
  0.8-scaled panel on a canvas that CanvasScaler "Expand" shrinks with
  the window (1536x1024 reference), so a 540-wide window drew it at 0.28.
  The pixels per unit are measured through the container's transform.
- bubbleSide "left"/"right": the bubble starts beside the avatar's head
  bone, projected through ME's camera (it draws both the avatar and the
  canvas), bubbleGap to the side and bubbleTop above it in metres at the
  avatar's scale, and grows downwards so the typing line stays put. It
  is narrowed to fit the window and follows the head sideways while
  ME's idle animations sway the avatar. No head bone: ME's spot.

The bubble log line now shows the size used and, with bubbleSide, the
head and corner positions; verbose also logs each mouth open/close.
Text-only lines (say + talk on, talk off later) needed no change.
