+
+**Size and placement.** ME parents its bubbles to the `TalkPanel` of the avatar's `AvatarRandomMessages`. That panel sits
+at a fixed spot left of the window's centre, on a canvas that scales with the window (`CanvasScaler` "Expand",
+1536x1024 reference: the scale is the smaller of width / 1536 and height / 1024), and the panel itself is scaled 0.8.
+So by default a bubble is drawn at 0.8 of its size in a 1536-wide window and about 0.28 in a 540-wide one, and it hangs
+left of the avatar, where a neighbouring avatar or the screen edge can cut it off.
+- `screenPixels` converts the configured sizes through that chain when each bubble is created, so the text has the
+  same size in any window.
+- `bubbleSide` projects the avatar's head bone to the screen through ME's camera, which draws both the avatar and the
+  canvas. The bubble then starts beside the head and grows downwards, so the first line stays put while the text types.
+  It is narrowed to fit when the window edge is closer than `bubbleWidth`, and its top is kept inside the window. ME's
+  idle animations sway the avatar by up to about a head's width, so the bubble follows the head sideways (smoothly,
+  never past the window edge) until it is removed. The offsets are in metres at the avatar's scale, so they fit any
+  window or avatar size. An avatar without a humanoid head bone falls back to ME's spot.
+- The size is fixed when each bubble is created. The log line `bubble shown on 'TalkPanel' (...)` shows it and, with
+  `bubbleSide`, the head's and the bubble corner's screen positions at that moment (pixels from the bottom left).
 
